# tally 2.1.8 L §6.1 l.1806, L §4.6 (B1 of group 4's review, agent/same_removed; refcore right, the engine's alone):
# a side of a same class whose readings are all removed by replace = none is no row, so last takes the class's
# latest kept reading, px[EUR]'s 4.3 at 2026-03-02.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
unit EUR: currency minor 0.01

input px[u in currencies]: num PLN/u reading
input qx[u in currencies]: num PLN/u reading

version r
  cite s
  known 2026-03-09
  px[EUR] = 4.3 PLN/EUR at 2026-03-02
  qx[EUR] = 4.4 PLN/EUR at 2026-03-08

version r2
  cite s
  known 2026-04-01
  replace qx[EUR] = none at 2026-03-08

version j
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  same px[EUR] = qx[EUR]

ask e: last(px[EUR], 2026-03-10), since(px[EUR], 2026-03-10)
ask q: last(qx[EUR], 2026-03-10), since(qx[EUR], 2026-03-10)
ask v: px[EUR] law 2026-03-08
=== expect
e: (4.3 PLN/EUR, 8)
  held: px[EUR] = 4.3 PLN/EUR (r), read for 2026-03-10
  cut 2026-12-31
q: (4.3 PLN/EUR, 8)
  held: px[EUR] = 4.3 PLN/EUR (r), read for 2026-03-10
  cut 2026-12-31
v: ?"px[EUR] has no reading at 2026-03-08" (px[EUR])
  law date 2026-03-08, cut 2026-12-31
